m "Consider a linear transformation $\\,T\\,.$ If $\\,{v}_{1}+{v}_{2}=0\\,$ and $\\,T({v}_{1})=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]\\,$, find $\\,T(9{v}_{1}-4{v}_{2}).$\n\n| $\\,T(9{v}_{1}-4{v}_{2})=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |\n|  | {{field-3}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, since ${v}_{1}+{v}_{2}=0,$ we have that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{v}_{1}-4{v}_{2} & =13{v}_{1}-4{v}_{1}-4{v}_{2} \\\\  & =13{v}_{1}-4({v}_{1}+{v}_{2}) \\\\  & =13{v}_{1}-4(0) \\\\  & =13{v}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nT(9{v}_{1}-4{v}_{2})=T(13{v}_{1}).\n$$\n\nNow, since $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that $T(kv)=kT(v).$ So \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(13{v}_{1}) & =13T({v}_{1}) \\\\  & =13[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-26 \\\\ 65 \\\\ -78\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn conclusion, $T(9{v}_{1}-4{v}_{2})=[\\begin{aligned}-26 \\\\ 65 \\\\ -78\\end{aligned}].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262633 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ad1c29f7-c0e7-5bed-944f-a2e33579c7b8" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Image of a Vector Under a Map Using the Scalar Multiplication Property"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9748f047-caec-5d27-bbfe-fab439fc719a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262635} {:answer/id #uuid "a7c959bd-b3d1-5e97-8069-ecd792c039c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262636} {:answer/id #uuid "74710f2a-9370-54c1-8e25-8c251ada75c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}14 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262637} {:answer/id #uuid "8c06956e-c0b1-570d-9b6d-888d3b86cd7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligne